Sure! Here's a simple CSS rule that centers a div both horizontally and vertically:

```css
div {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
```

This centers the div in the middle of the viewport.

Alternatively, for a more modern and flexible approach using Flexbox:

```css
div {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
  height: 100%; /* or set a specific height */
}
```

This will center the div both horizontally and vertically within its container.
